    244                             "Error creating sprite %1!s!."
    245                             "Perspective view:  To move along the XZ plane, press and hold the I key while moving the mouse.  To move along the Y axis, press and hold the I key and the RMB while moving the mouse.  To change orientation, press and hold the O key and move the mouse.\r\n\r\nParallel view:  To move along the plane, press and hold the I key while moving the mouse.  To zoom in and out, press and hold the O key while moving the mouse.\r\n\r\nTo find the cursor's current position, watch the status bar.\r\n\r\nTo change the green marker's position, press and hold the X key while moving the mouse in the parallel views.  The green marker is used to define positions for new objects and the origin for new brushes.\r\n\r\n"
    246                             "To define a brush, first move the green marker to where the top polygon of the brush is to be.  You must do this in a view perpendicular to the top polygon.  Then define the vertices of the top polygon by moving the cursor and pressing the space bar.  Once the polygon is closed, define the height of the brush.  The other polygons will be extruded from the top polygon.\r\n\r\nTo place a new object, first move the green marker to the object's position.  Then select World|Add Object...  Select the object from the class heirarchy.\r\n\r\nTo select a brush, move the cursor over the brush, press and hold the T key, then click the LMB.  Clicking the LMB repeatedly cycles to the next brush under the cursor.\r\n\r\nTo select an object, first select Object Edit mode from the toolbar.  Then move the cursor over the object.  Then press and hold the T key.  Finally, click the LMB.\r\n\r\n"
    247                             "To move a brush or an object, first select it.  Then press and hold the M key and LMB, while moving the mouse.\r\n\r\nTo texture a brush, first select it.  Then select the texture from the Textures tab.  Finally, click Apply Texture button on the toolbar."
    248                             "View"
    249                             "Description"
    250                             "All"
    251                             "Geometry"
    252                             "Brush"
    253                             "Spacebar"
    254                             "Ctrl+"
    255                             "Shift+"
END

